# Subagents

- Default model for every subagent (Task tool `model`) is `grok-4.7-xhigh-fast`:
  extra-high reasoning, fast tier. Do not fall back to `inherit`, a `high` tier
  or another family unless Jakob asks for it in that turn.
- Context: Jakob wants the 500k window. The Task tool rejects the
  `[context=500k]` suffix (verified 2026-10-07), so the window follows the
  model's own default. A custom agent in `.cursor/agents/*.md` may declare
  `model: grok-4.7-xhigh-fast[context=500k]` in its frontmatter; prefer that
  when one exists. Never shrink a brief to save tokens.
- Give each subagent the full brief; never shrink the prompt to save tokens.
- The orchestrator (this chat) reviews, validates and merges. Subagents never
  commit, push, create branches, run migrations or touch production.
- Every subagent report ends with a section titled `Tveksamt` listing each
  decision Jakob should see before merge. Nothing doubtful is merged without
  his word.
- Nothing may get worse: no removed link, action or page a user can reach
  today. A red existing test is reverted, not rewritten to pass.
